#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138211 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138458 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "010539bb-ae6a-5071-a7bd-25c40d5a9717" :knowledge-point/title "Choosing Appropriate Units When Base Units Are Required"}] :question/id #uuid "f0782388-8184-5922-8e9e-d9edcf727264" :question/math-academy-id "e-1526" :question/problem "Density $D$ is the rate that mass $M$ changes as volume $V$ changes. What are the units of density in terms of base units?" :question/worked-solution "We *measure the change* in the mass, as *we change* the volume. Consequently, any appropriate unit must take the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{unit of mass}}{\\textrm{unit of volume}}\n$$\n\nThe base unit for mass is $\\textrm{kg}$, and the base unit for volume is $\\textrm{m}^3$. Therefore, the units of density are\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{kg}}{\\textrm{m}^3}\n$$\n\nor, kilograms per cubic meter."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138313 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138440 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86db8dde-c4ad-5ba3-9022-afe85acbc3d8" :knowledge-point/title "Choosing Appropriate Units When Base Units Are Not Required"}] :question/id #uuid "66c31f3c-2abb-51ff-b8d5-8377aeb90d80" :question/math-academy-id "e-901" :question/problem "A tank is being filled with water. What is an appropriate unit for measuring the rate of change of water volume in the tank, as time goes on?" :question/worked-solution "We *measure the change* of the volume as *we change* the amount of time. Consequently, any appropriate unit for measuring the rate of change of water volume in the tank must take the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{unit of volume}}{\\textrm{unit of time}}\n$$\n\nSome examples of appropriate units include\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{liters}}{\\textrm{hour}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{m}^3}{\\textrm{min}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{cm}^3}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$"}]}
